config BR2_PACKAGE_XR871_BRIDGE
	bool "XR871 co-processor keep-alive daemon"
	help
	  xr871d speaks the UART control protocol of the XR871 WiFi
	  co-processor used on some Ingenic battery cameras (e.g. ABUS
	  PPIC90520). It sends the heartbeat the XR871 expects, answers
	  its requests and takes the wall clock from it. Without it the
	  XR871 power-cycles the main SoC a few seconds after boot.

	  It is started from rcF (F00xr871d) right after the sysinit mounts.
